      "message": "[error] Line 97: 🔴 `stop()` unconditionally calls `context.unregisterReceiver(receiver)`. If shutdown paths call `terminateDaemon()` more than once (or if `start()` failed/was skipped), this throws `IllegalArgumentException` and can crash process teardown. Track a `started/registered` flag (set only after successful registration) and make `stop()` idempotent, or catch `IllegalArgumentException` here like you already do for network callback unregistration.",
